          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong Monster group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
            that is the largest of the
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sporadic+finite+simple+group"} sporadic finite simple group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order+of+a+group"} order
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mn 2
                            %mn 46
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msup
                            %mn 3
                            %mn 20
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msup
                            %mn 5
                            %mn 9
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msup
                            %mn 7
                            %mn 6
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msup
                            %mn 11
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msup
                            %mn 13
                            %mn 3
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mn 17
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mn 19
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mn 23
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mn 29
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mn 31
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mn 41
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mn 47
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mn 59
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mn 71
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mn 808017424794512875886459904961710757005754368000000000
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \&amp; 2^{46}\cdot 3^{20}\cdot 5^9\cdot 7^6\cdot 11^2\cdot 13^3\cdot 17\cdot 19\cdot 23\cdot 29\cdot 31\cdot 41\cdot 47\cdot 59\cdot 71
                  \\\
                  \&amp; = 808017424794512875886459904961710757005754368000000000
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            and contains all but six (the ‘
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pariah+groups"}> pariah groups
            ’) of the other 25
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sporadic+finite+simple+groups"} sporadic finite simple groups
            as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subquotients"} subquotients
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Happy+Family"} Happy Family
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moonshine"} Moonshine
          %h2#history History
          %p
            The Monster group was predicted to exist by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernd+Fischer"} Bernd Fischer
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Griess"} Robert Griess
            in 1973, as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+group"} simple group
            containing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fischer+groups"} Fischer groups
            and some other sporadic simple groups as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subquotients"} subquotients
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            and discovered other properties and subgroups, assuming that it existed. In a famous paper
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Griess"}> Robert Griess
              ,
              %em The Friendly Giant
              , Inventiones (1982)
          %p
            Griess proved the existence of the largest simple sporadic group. The author constructs “by hand” a non-associative but commutative algebra of dimension 196883, and showed that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
            of this algebra is the conjectured friendly giant/monster simple group. The name “Friendly Giant” for the Monster did not take on.
          %p
            After Griess found this algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Frenkel"} Igor Frenkel
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Lepowsky"} James Lepowsky
            and Meurman and/or Borcherds showed that the Griess algebra is just the degree 2 part of the infinite dimensional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moonshine+vertex+algebra"} Moonshine vertex algebra
          %p
            There is a school of thought, going back to at least
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Israel+Gelfand"} Israel Gelfand
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2006/09/mathematical_kinds.html"} this nCafe post
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moonshine"} Moonshine
            phenomena) is that what we know as the Monster is just a shadow of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"} 2-group
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theory"} conformal field theory
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2008/10/john_mckay_visits_kent.html#c019440"} this nCafe discussion
          %h2#presentation Presentation
          %h3#via_coxeter_groups Via Coxeter groups
          %p
            The Monster admits a reasonably succinct description in terms of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coxeter+groups"} Coxeter groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
            denote the linear
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"} graph
            with vertices
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0, 1, \ldots, n
            with an edge between adjacent numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi i
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i, i+1
            and no others. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            is the terminal (1-element) graph, there is a map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0: 1 \to [n]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            to the vertex
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/undercategory"} undercategory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi Graph
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \downarrow Graph
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mn 443
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_{443}
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            of the three objects
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0: 1 \to [4]
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0: 1 \to [4]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0: 1 \to [3]
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi Graph
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \downarrow Graph
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
          %p
            Regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mn 443
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_{443}
            as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coxeter+diagram"} Coxeter diagram
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coxeter+group"} Coxeter group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 443
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{443}
            is given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+presentation"} group presentation
            with 12 generators (represented by the vertices) of order
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            (so 12 relators of the form
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^2 = 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mi y
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 3
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x y)^3 = 1
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y
            are adjacent vertices (so 11 relators, one for each edge), and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mi y
                  %mo =
                  %mi y
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y = y x
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y
            are non-adjacent (55 more relators). This Coxeter group (12 generators, 78 relators) is infinite, but by modding out by another strange ‘spider’ relator
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 3
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 3
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 10
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a b_1 c_1 a b_2 c_2 a b_3 c_3)^{10} = 1
          %p
            the resulting quotient
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            turns out to be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            is the central vertex of valence
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_1, c_1
            are on an arm of length
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_1
            adjacent to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1 \neq a
            adjacent to
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_2, c_2
            on the other arm of length
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_3, c_3
            on the arm of length
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            %a{:href => "http://www.maths.qmul.ac.uk/~jnb/web/Pres/Mnst.html"} here
            if this is not clear.
          %p
            It turns out that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/center"} center
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            of order
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is the quotient, i.e. the indicated term in the exact sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi N
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \to C \to N \to M \to 1.
          %p This implicitly describes the Monster in terms of 12 generators and 80 relators.
          %p
            Such “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            \-group” presentations (Coxeter group based on a similar
            = succeed "-diagram," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mn 555
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_{555}
            which is a presentation of the “Bimonster” (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wreath+product"} wreath product
            of the Monster with
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
            %a{:href => "#Iv"} Ivanov
            for a general description of these. The presentation of the Monster given above was established in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Iv2"} Ivanov2
          %h3#ViaAutomorphisms Via automorphisms of a super vertex operator algebra
          %p
            There is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vertex+operator+algebra"} super vertex operator algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Monster+vertex+operator+algebra"} Monster vertex operator algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} group of
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphisms+of+a+VOA"} automorphisms of a VOA
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monster+group"} monster group
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#FrenkelLepowskiMeurman89"}> Frenkel-Lepowski-Meurman 89
